 "sections": [
  {
   "heading": "Contents",
   "level": 2,
   "text": ""
  },
  {
   "heading": "Theory",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "55edo can be used for a meantone tuning, and is close to 1/6-comma meantone (and is almost exactly 10/57-comma meantone). Telemann suggested it as a theoretical basis for analyzing the intervals of meantone . Leopold and Wolfgang Mozart recommended 55edo or something close to it, with a subset and further approximation used for keyboard instruments which (apart from an experimental instrument) did not have enough notes per octave to accommodate it in full. [ 1 ] It can also be used for Mohajira and Liese temperaments. It also supports an extremely sharp tuning of Huygens/undecimal meantone using the 55de val , meaning that primes 7 and 11 are mapped very sharply to their second-best mapping."
  },
  {
   "heading": "Odd harmonics",
   "level": 3,
   "text": ""
  },
  {
   "heading": "Subsets and supersets",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Since 55 factors into 5 × 11 , 55edo contains 5edo and 11edo as its subsets."
  },
  {
   "heading": "Intervals",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "* 55f val (tending flat), inconsistent intervals labeled in italic"
  },
